error[E0277]: this subscriber has no batches to size
  --> tests/ui/subscriber_batch_without_a_slice_body.rs:19:26
   |
19 |     let _capped = handle.batch(nonzero!(64));
   |                          ^^^^^ `batch(..)` sizes the batches a batch body is handed
   |
   = help: the trait `ruststream::runtime::CapsBatches` is not implemented for `HandleValue<Solo<Order>, (), (), (), handle, ruststream::runtime::Probed>`
   = note: the batch size belongs to a batch body (`&[T]`, `&[F<'_>]`, `&[Message<H, P>]`); a single-message body takes no batch, and how many of those are in flight at once is `workers(n)` instead
   = help: the following other types implement trait `ruststream::runtime::CapsBatches`:
             HandleValue<BatchCarried<T>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
             HandleValue<BatchDeserialized<F>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
             HandleValue<BatchPair<Hd, P>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
             HandleValue<BatchSet<S>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
             HandleValue<ruststream::runtime::Batch<T>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
   = note: required for `Sealed<HandleValue<Solo<Order>, (), (), (), handle, ruststream::runtime::Probed>>` to implement `ruststream::runtime::CapsBatches`
   = note: required for `SubscriberBuilder<Sealed<HandleValue<Solo<Order>, (), (), (), handle, ruststream::runtime::Probed>>, Name, (Open, Open, Open, Open)>` to implement `BatchStep`
